<title>UK: INTERVIEW - T&amp;L sees brighter Staley future.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - T&amp;L sees brighter Staley future.</headline>
<byline>Tim Farrand</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Larry Pillard, chief executive of British sugar and starch producer Tate and Lyle, said on Wednesday the company's beleagured North American unit Staley should benefit from improved market conditions this year.</p>
<p>&quot;Conditions have reversed this year so that corn milling companies can divert some of their excess capacity into ethanol and that could tighten up the market a bit,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Wet corn miller Staley posted a 50 percent fall in earnings because of a record increase in maize costs, dragging down group pretax profits for the year by some 35 million to 276.3 million.</p>
</text>
